``` HL-0007 - Inhibit System Recovery: shadow copy, backup catalog and boot recovery tampering (ATT&CK T1490) ```
``` Platform: Splunk. Sources: Sysmon EventCode 1 and/or Windows Security EventCode 4688 (command-line auditing required) ```
``` Playbook: playbooks/HL-0007-T1490-inhibit-system-recovery.md ```
``` A hit in the last hour is an IR trigger, not just a hunt lead (see playbook section 4) ```
``` Adjust index/sourcetype and field names to match your Windows TA / CIM mapping ```
``` Lab dataset: use earliest=0 ```
index=windows (EventCode=1 OR EventCode=4688) earliest=-14d
| eval proc=coalesce(Image, New_Process_Name, NewProcessName),
       cmd=coalesce(CommandLine, Process_Command_Line),
       parent=coalesce(ParentImage, Creator_Process_Name, ParentProcessName),
       parent_cmd=coalesce(ParentCommandLine, parent),
       acct=coalesce(User, Account_Name, user),
       dest=coalesce(Computer, ComputerName, host)
| rex field=proc "(?<proc_name>[^\\\\]+)$"
| rex field=parent "(?<parent_name>[^\\\\]+)$"
| eval proc_name=lower(proc_name), parent_name=lower(parent_name)
| eval action=case(
    proc_name="vssadmin.exe" AND match(cmd, "(?i)(delete shadows|resize shadowstorage)"), "vssadmin shadow delete/resize",
    proc_name="wmic.exe" AND match(cmd, "(?i)shadowcopy") AND match(cmd, "(?i)delete"), "wmic shadowcopy delete",
    match(cmd, "(?i)win32_shadowcopy") AND match(cmd, "(?i)delete"), "Win32_ShadowCopy delete",
    proc_name="bcdedit.exe" AND match(cmd, "(?i)(recoveryenabled no|bootstatuspolicy ignoreallfailures)"), "bcdedit recovery disabled",
    proc_name="wbadmin.exe" AND match(cmd, "(?i)delete") AND match(cmd, "(?i)(catalog|systemstatebackup|backup)"), "wbadmin delete",
    true(), null())
| where isnotnull(action)
``` Destructive scope (/all, -quiet, recovery off) vs. housekeeping (/oldest on one volume) ```
| eval broad_scope=if(match(cmd, "(?i)(/all|-quiet)") OR action="bcdedit recovery disabled" OR action="wbadmin delete", 1, 0)
| stats count AS hits dc(action) AS distinct_actions values(action) AS actions dc(dest) AS hosts values(dest) AS host_list
        sum(broad_scope) AS broad_scope_hits min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen values(cmd) AS sample_cmds
        BY parent_name parent_cmd acct
| eval span_minutes=round((last_seen-first_seen)/60, 0), host_list=mvindex(host_list, 0, 24), sample_cmds=mvindex(sample_cmds, 0, 9)
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
``` Ransomware pattern first: many distinct actions from one parent, then multi-host, then rare ```
| sort 0 -distinct_actions -hosts hits
``` Pivot: index=windows (EventCode=1 OR EventCode=4688) on the same hosts and account (or CommandLine/ParentCommandLine="<parent_cmd>" on any host), -1h/+2h - this is how you find the encryptor and the spread ```
